{"tag":"J7D1","kind":"definition","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"dfn-1","file":"","number":"1.1","order":1,"title":"Definition","body_md":"{\\upshape\n\n By a {\\em long virtual knot diagram} we mean a smooth\nimmersion $f:\\mathbb{R}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}^2$ such that:\n\n\\noindent 1) outside some big circle, we have $f(t)=(t,0)$;\n\n\\noindent 2) each intersection point is double and transverse;\n\n\\noindent 3) each intersection point is endowed with classical (with\na choice for underpass and overpass specified) or virtual crossing\nstructure. }","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"dfn","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"dfn","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":71,"to":84},"hash":"sha256:a3b6cf5221bba9b60467061442c1bf5ec29d107ce91af8e7e2f88c20aa1078cf","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"G2O7","kind":"definition","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"dfn-2","file":"","number":"1.2","order":2,"title":"Definition","body_md":"{\\upshape\n  A {\\em long virtual knot} is an equivalence class of long virtual\n  knot diagrams modulo generalized Reidemeister moves.\n  }","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"dfn","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"dfn","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":88,"to":93},"hash":"sha256:547ad01767c2b7df47597e30a456c5d5f05765253d6bdd845b519f5c0826d9d0","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"5KRU","kind":"definition","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"dfn-3","file":"","number":"1.3","order":3,"title":"Definition","body_md":"{\\upshape By an {\\em arc} of a long virtual knot diagram we mean a\nconnected component of the set, obtained from the diagram by\ndeleting all virtual crossings (at classical crossing the\nundercrossing pair of edges of the diagram is thought to be disjoint\nas it is usually illustrated). }","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"dfn","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"dfn","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":95,"to":101},"hash":"sha256:afe6ba35ed54269200e575c8329f570ac05cfa85b942a90538b1697faf3e550d","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"JIQB","kind":"definition","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"dfn-4","file":"","number":"1.4","order":4,"title":"Definition","body_md":"{\\upshape\n We say that two arcs $a, a'$ belong to the same {\\em long\narc} if there exists a sequence of arcs $a = a_{1},\\dots,  a_{n+1} =\na'$ and virtual crossings $c_{1},\\dots,c_{n}$ such that for $i =\n1,\\dots, n$ the arcs $a_{i},a_{i+1}$ are incident to $c_i$ from\nopposite sides. }","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"dfn","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"dfn","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":103,"to":110},"hash":"sha256:ba2fda48e207b1e5a48eb4f5d7e61c1ecbbe2d5898d37350179f1a195ee5c090","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"A5C2","kind":"definition","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"dfn-5","file":"","number":"1.5","order":5,"title":"Definition","body_md":"{\\upshape\n An {\\em incidence coefficient}\n $[v:a]\\in T=\\mathbb{Z}[p,p^{-1},q,q^{-1}]/((p-1)(p-q),(q-1)(p-q))$ of classical\ncrossing $v$ and arc $a$ is defined as a sum of some of three\npolynomials: $[v:a]={\\varepsilon}_1 1+{\\varepsilon}_2\n(t^{sgn\\,v}-1)+{\\varepsilon}_3(-t^{sgn\\,v})$, where\n${\\varepsilon}_i\\in\\{0,1\\},i=1,2,3$; $t=p$ if $v$ is early\novercrossing, $t=q$ if $v$ is early undercrossing; $sgn\\,v$ denotes\n{\\em local writhe number} of $v$. We set\n${\\varepsilon}_1=1\\Leftrightarrow$ arc $a$ is emanating from $v$;\n ${\\varepsilon}_2=1\\Leftrightarrow$ $a$ is passing over $v$;\n ${\\varepsilon}_3=1\\Leftrightarrow$ $a$ is coming into $v$.\n\\noindent If $v$ and $a$ are not incident we set $[v:a]=0$.\n }","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"dfn","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"dfn","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":126,"to":141},"hash":"sha256:0a56325140efbe35de359d5d2d70f75efa681460987d85e4405814ef02903fc6","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"YK1W","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"thm-1","file":"","label":"theorem0","number":"1.1","order":6,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{theorem0}\n If virtual diagrams $D,D^{\\prime}$ are equivalent then $\\zeta(D^{\\prime})=q^{r}\\zeta(D)$\n for some integer $r$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["theorem0"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"here","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":169,"to":172},"hash":"sha256:49995eab9849836a54ac981665297ba7d61f535de12939cda0295e1529807d7e","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"S3A9","kind":"proof","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"proof-1","file":"","order":7,"title":"Proof","body_md":"The invariance of $\\zeta$ for Reidemeister moves\n$\\Omega_1^{\\prime},\\Omega_2^{\\prime},\\Omega_3^{\\prime}$ is evident.\nThe checking of invariance for $\\Omega^{\\prime}$ and $\\Omega_2$\n is similar to the case of $\\zeta$-polynomial\nfor virtual link (see \\cite{MyBookEng},\\cite{MyBook}).\n\nThere are two types of the first Reidemeister move $\\Omega_1$:\n${\\Omega}_1^p$, if we have early overcrossing, and ${\\Omega}_1^q$,\nif we have early undercrossing. It easy to calculate that\n$\\zeta({\\Omega}_1^p(D))=\\zeta(D)$, $\\zeta({\\Omega}_1^q(D))=q^{\\pm\n1}\\zeta(D)$.\n\nIt is convenient to use the Laplace theorem (about determinants) to\ncheck that $det\\, A(\\Omega_3(D))=det\\,A(D)$. We check equality for\n$10$ pair of $3\\times3$-minors of matrices $A(\\Omega_3(D))$ and\n$det\\,A(D)$. Two of these pairs give equalities only if we set\n$(p-1)(p-q)=0,(q-1)(p-q)=0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proof","item":"proof","head":"environment","name":"A sketch of the proof","scope":"paper","proves":"thm-1","attach":3,"span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":173,"to":192},"hash":"sha256:a428d4ed8c5801c13386bf713a66737375a0bf360b8cc09c41369c2f67f104f1","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#proof-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"S11W","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"thm-2","file":"","label":"theorem1","number":"1.2","order":8,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{theorem1} Let $k$ be the number\nof virtual crossings on a long virtual diagram $D$. Then\n$deg_s\\,\\zeta(D)\\leqslant k$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["theorem1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":196,"to":199},"hash":"sha256:e2bc60f866289d669849668be8a7e513edd2ed6fa74ce4561c1554f7e197fbc3","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"RM39","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"cor-1","file":"","label":"cor1","number":"1.1","order":9,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"\\label{cor1}\nIf\\, $deg_s\\,\\zeta(D)=k$ then $D$ has minimal virtual crossing\nnumber.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"cor","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"cor","number_from":"counter","labels":["cor1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":203,"to":206},"hash":"sha256:3f0f77241bb52b211970911c768864c29299ee2bcc5537be132e3e12d954be9b","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"LXIT","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"thm-3","file":"","label":"theorem3","number":"1.3","order":10,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{theorem3} The $s^k$-th coefficient of\\, $\\zeta(D)$ is\nequal to $det\\,B$, where $B_{ij}=[v_i:a_j]$ if\\, $\\exists\\,\na_j\\subset{\\gamma}^j$ s.t. $deg\\,a_j=$\\#of increasing virtual\ncrossings on $\\gamma^j$, and $B_{ij}=0$ otherwise, $i,j=1,...,n$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["theorem3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":211,"to":215},"hash":"sha256:fabc9ccb1abb16920bfefe778bfd8bd589ee76166f9c3bd3383fc5903038d4c4","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-9","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"08RQ","kind":"remark","subkind":"example","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"head-1","file":"","order":11,"title":"Example","body_md":"In {\\bf Figure} we draw long virtual diagram\n$D_{r,l}$ which closure is unknot. Arcs $a_j$, $j=1,...,n$, are\nmarked by thick lines. By Theorem \\ref{theorem3} the $s^k$-th\ncoefficient of\\, $\\zeta(D)$ is equal to $|[v_i:a_j]|_{i,j=1,...,n}=$\n$q^{r+l}(qp^{-1}-1)=q-p\\neq 0$ in the ring $T$. Consequently,\n$D_{r,l}$ is minimal by Corollary \\ref{cor1}.","path":"source","confidence":"medium","env":"head","item":"example","head":"manual","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":217,"to":222},"hash":"sha256:a49fbecff2ab36f38d98b5b15465ed8633f27b2dd125ecb3c042c65a46108bcb","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#head-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"KVG1","kind":"problem","subkind":"conjecture","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"head-2","file":"","order":12,"title":"Conjecture","body_md":"{\\em If $D$ is a minimal long\nvirtual diagram with respect number of virtual crossings, K is a\nlong classical knot diagram, then $D*K$ is also minimal.}","path":"source","confidence":"medium","env":"head","item":"conjecture","head":"manual","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":235,"to":237},"hash":"sha256:28e523e242568b82c748d13678e517b257402bd377ca5276befd1b8ed67a9888","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#head-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"9EQ8","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"thm-4","file":"","label":"theorem2","number":"1.4","order":13,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{theorem2}(the particular case of Conjecture)\\\\\nIf $D$ is a minimal long virtual diagram s.t. $deg_s\\,\\zeta(D)$ is\nequal to virtual crossing number of $D$, $K$ is a long classical\nknot diagram, then $D*K$ is minimal.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["theorem2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"here","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":241,"to":245},"hash":"sha256:a49b71363f4003176c5f181d8e40dc5b475490595440b01b2548dbf638e3d1ec","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-10","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"NYJ4","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"lem-1","file":"","label":"lem1","number":"1.1","order":14,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lem1}\n  $\\zeta_{-}(D_1*D_2)=-\\zeta_{-}(D_1)\\zeta_{-}(D_2)$;\n   $\\zeta_{+}(D_1*D_2)=\\zeta_{+}(D_1)\\zeta_{+}(D_2)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lem","number_from":"counter","labels":["lem1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":262,"to":265},"hash":"sha256:1ffb715a9306da97f583c5a7b9342b2a46f3f665c30b150000a1a5caff7b6004","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-11","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"WF85","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"lem-2","file":"","label":"lem2","number":"1.2","order":15,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lem2}\n  $x\\in T=\\mathbb{Z}[p,p^{-1},q,q^{-1}]/((p-1)(p-q),(q-1)(p-q))$ is\n  zero divisor $\\Leftrightarrow$ $x|_{p=1,\\,q=1}=0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lem","number_from":"counter","labels":["lem2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":267,"to":270},"hash":"sha256:275c7c90119aa3b7df854ca16b36e5ebb72c8b685d9e98a630de4f714dc105ba","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#env-12","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
{"tag":"27PB","kind":"proof","paper":"0906.4245","version":"1","local":"proof-2","file":"","order":16,"title":"Proof","body_md":"By Lemma \\ref{lem1}\\, $\\zeta(D*K)=\\zeta_{-}(D*K)+\\zeta_{+}(D*K)=$\n$-\\zeta_{-}(D)\\zeta_{-}(K)+\\zeta_{+}(D)\\zeta_{+}(K)=$\n$\\zeta_{+}(K)\\zeta(D)$, because $\\zeta(K)=0$. Consequently,\n$deg_s\\,\\zeta(D*K)=deg_s\\,\\zeta(D)$ if $\\zeta_{+}(K)\\in T$ is not\nzero divisor.\n\nIt easy to check that $\\zeta_{+}(K)|_{p=1,\\,q=1}=\\pm\n\\Delta(K)|_{t=1}$, where $\\Delta$ denotes Alexander polynomial. It\nis known that $\\Delta(K)|_{t=1}=\\pm 1$. Hence, by Lemma \\ref{lem2}\\,\n$\\zeta_{+}(K)$ is not zero divisor, because\n$\\zeta_{+}(K)|_{p=1,\\,q=1}\\neq 0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proof","item":"proof","head":"environment","scope":"paper","proves":"thm-4","attach":1,"span":{"file":"estimates.tex","from":272,"to":285},"hash":"sha256:727c4ac82beaf44e3ebf7144d243b35ad7b2742aac39de5d2c069389392869b9","minhash":"","census":"0906.4245v1#proof-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.17"}
